    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "If the residuals follow a multivariate normal distribution, $ \\mathbf{e} \\sim \\text{MVN}(0, \\mathbf{V}) $, and $ \\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{X}\\boldsymbol{\\beta} + \\mathbf{e} $ is indeed the correct model, then $ \\mathbf{y} - \\hat{\\mathbf{y}} \\sim \\text{MVN}(0, \\mathbf{V}) $ and it follows from Equation A3.9 that",
      "source_page": 854,
